---
import { site } from "../../lib/site";

/* SPEC §4c — before and after on four measures, marked illustrative in the
   body at body size, because these are not a named client's measurements.
   Hardening is the service we lead with, so the four weeks are spelled out. */
const rows = [
  { metric: "p95 API response", before: "2400ms", after: "280ms", note: "Index audit, N+1 removal, connection pooling" },
  { metric: "Error rate", before: "3%", after: "0.4%", note: "Structured logging, then fixing what it showed" },
  { metric: "Integration tests", before: "0", after: "140", note: "Covering the path that takes the money" },
  { metric: "Deploys", before: "1/month", after: "9/week", note: "CI, migrations and a rollback that has been used" },
];

const weeks = [
  ["Week 1", "Audit", "We read the codebase, the logs and the support inbox, reproduce the worst bugs, and agree with you the four numbers that define stable for your product."],
  ["Week 2", "Fix what hurts users", "Crashes, failed payments, broken sign ups and slow pages come first, each one fixed with a test that stops it coming back."],
  ["Week 3", "Tests, security and speed", "Automated tests across every critical flow, a security pass on authentication, data access and dependencies, and performance work on the slowest screens."],
  ["Week 4", "Release and handover", "CI/CD, monitoring and alerts in place, a production release you can roll back, and a runbook so your team or ours can keep it stable."],
];
---

<section class="v5-section" id="v5-hardening" aria-labelledby="v5-hard-title">
  <div class="v5-container">
    <header class="v5-head">
      <div>
        <p class="v5-label">Product hardening from $1,999</p>
        <h2 class="v5-h2" id="v5-hard-title">It is live, and it keeps falling<br />over. We fix that in four weeks.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="v5-head__aside">
        For software that already has users: built quickly, by an earlier developer or an AI
        coding tool, and now failing under real traffic. We fix it, test it and make releases
        safe, so you can market it with confidence.
        <a class="v5-link v5-head__link" href={site.booking}>Book a hardening call</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <ol class="v5-hard-weeks" data-v5-reveal="drop" data-v5-stagger>
      {
        weeks.map(([when, title, body]) => (
          <li class="v5-card">
            <span class="v5-card__n">{when}</span>
            <h3 class="v5-card__title">{title}</h3>
            <p class="v5-card__body">{body}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <p class="v5-illustrative">
      Four numbers have to move before we call it stable. The figures below are illustrative:
      the shape of a typical four week engagement, not measurements from a named client. We
      agree your own four numbers in week one and report them every Friday.
    </p>

    <div class="v5-readout" role="table" aria-label="Before and after, illustrative" data-v5-reveal="fade">
      <div class="v5-readout__row v5-readout__row--head" role="row">
        <span role="columnheader">Measure</span>
        <span role="columnheader">Before</span>
        <span role="columnheader">After</span>
        <span role="columnheader">What moved it</span>
      </div>
      {
        rows.map((r) => (
          <div class="v5-readout__row" role="row">
            <span role="cell" class="v5-readout__metric">{r.metric}</span>
            <span role="cell" class="v5-readout__before">{r.before}</span>
            <span role="cell" class="v5-readout__after">{r.after}</span>
            <span role="cell" class="v5-readout__note">{r.note}</span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
